## Layout

- `html { scroll-snap-type: y mandatory; scroll-behavior: smooth; }`
- Each `<section>` = `min-height: 100vh`, scroll-snap, padding `80px 60px 60px`, fades up on intersection (`section.visible` class).
- `.inner { max-width: 880px; }` for left-aligned content; `.centered` modifier for centered sections.
- Section background: `radial-gradient(ellipse at 30% 40%, rgba(59,130,246,0.25) 0%, #07162C 60%)` for hero + standard sections.

## Required UI elements

- **Progress bar.** `.progress-bar` fixed top 3px, gradient `#1241B0 → #3b82f6`, width = `(activeIdx + 1) / activeCount`.
- **Nav dots.** `.nav-dots` fixed right-center. `.nav-dot` 8px, hover tooltip with `data-title`. Active = `#3b82f6` glow + 1.4× scale.
- **Section sorter.** Modal opened with `M`. Each section gets a card with title, current marker, skip toggle. Skipped sections hidden during presentation. State persisted in `localStorage` keyed by document title.
- **Skip badge.** `K` toggles skip on current section. `SKIPPED` chip appears bottom-right when current section is skipped.
- **Help hint.** Bottom-right text: `↑ ↓ navigate · K skip section · M section sorter`.
- **Keyboard nav.** Arrow Down / Right / Space → next active. Arrow Up / Left → previous active.

## Reusable section components

- **`.hero`** — large radial-gradient title slide. Logo top, `.section-label` ("Module N — AI Product Management Certification"), `<h1>The <span>...</span></h1>` (span is white on blue h1 / blue on white-h1), subtitle, 3 `.waypoint` cards, `Out:` line, scroll hint.
- **`.expect-grid` / `.expect-card`** — 6-icon "How This Module Runs" panel (replaces the strategy course's "Class Expectations"). Icons + title + 1-line desc.
- **`.arc-flow`** — horizontal strip of 6 `.arc-node` (one per module) + `.arc-arrow` between. Active module gets `.active-node` + 2px border in section accent. Use these short labels in nodes (consistent with `juno-project-template/` folder names): `Prompting`, `Strategy`, `RAG / PRD`, `AI-UX`, `Agentic`, `Evals`.
- **`.tf-grid` / `.tf-item`** — provocation thumb-vote panel. `.tf-verdict` shows `?` until clicked, then `TRUE`/`FALSE`/`PARTIAL`. Body has `.tf-claim` + `.tf-why` (hidden until revealed).
- **`.case-acts`** — 3-act case study: `.act-bet` (blue), `.act-crack` (gold), `.act-correct` (green).
- **`.waypoints` / `.waypoint`** — numbered list cards with `.waypoint-num` (white digit on blue square) + `.waypoint-text`.
- **`.evidence-cards`** — 2-up cards with label + company + text. Used for examples and extra practice.
- **`section.section-break`** — full-bleed lab header. `.lab-title` (small caps) + `.lab-name` (52px Poppins) + `.lab-desc`.
- **`.split-section` (`.split-left` + `.split-right`)** — large 45/55 split. Used for Build Moments. Right pane has soft white panel; left has `.lab-badge` + `.lab-timer` + `.lab-goal` + `.lab-tip`.
- **`.lab-timer`** — top-right pill showing `⏰ N min` for applied-work sections.
- **`.demo-tag`** — pill-tag at top of section indicating section type: `Provocation`, `Lecture · X`, `Case Study`, `Applied Work`, etc.
- **`.bottom-cta`** — full-width footer banner inside an applied-work section. Repo CTA button + repo path.
- **`.takeaway-list` / `.takeaway-item`** — closing-slide bullets with bold lead.
- **`.artifact-preview`** — outlined blue card showing what gets committed.
- **`.complete-stats`** — 3-up stat cards on a closing slide.
- **`.debrief-box`** — purple-outline slide for reflection prompts.

## Per-deck structure (canonical M1–M6 flow)

Recommended order:

1. **Hero** with 3 waypoints + `Out:` line.
2. **How This Module Runs** (6 expect-cards — solo format).
3. **The Course Arc** (arc-flow, current module active).
4. **Recall / Scenario** — for M1: "RocketShip is in Signal Collapse." For M2–M6: "What you brought from M{N-1}" with green-check waypoints.
5. **Provocation** — TF panel of 3 claims.
6. **Lecture(s)** — domain-specific frameworks. Use cards/tables/diag-axes.
7. **Section break** — "Lab 1: …".
8. **Applied Work** — Open the M{N} tool, with `.lab-timer`, table or fields, repo CTA.
9. **Break ☕**.
10. **Case Study** — 3-act real-world example.
11. More lectures + applied work.
12. **Synthesis** — "Your Repo After Today" with `.arc-flow` of folders.
13. **Bridge to next module** — arc-flow with next module as active.
14. **Key Takeaways** — `.takeaway-list`, 3–5 items.
15. **Extra Practice** — `.evidence-cards`, 2 items.
16. **Q&A**.

## Instructor vs. shareable

- **Instructor (`Module {N} - Slides.html`):** includes `.notes` blocks per slide with `<h4>Speaker Notes</h4>` + prose for the instructor. Notes use blue left-border, dark blue background.
- **Shareable (`Module {N} - Slides (Shareable).html`):** instructor notes stripped. Section count and structure otherwise identical. Replace `.notes` with `.takeaway` (cyan left-border, summary line) where the underlying point would otherwise be lost.

## Voice

- Confident. Opinionated. Direct. No corporate softening.
- Apply `individual-only-voice.mdc` — solo throughout. No peer/pair/group.
- One concept per slide. Never two.
- Keep paragraphs ≤2 sentences inside slides.

## Closing slide

Every module deck ends with **Q&A** preceded by **Key Takeaways** (3–5 takeaway-items) and an **Extra Practice** card.
